# Case of the Gateway Express: "When this Case enters, choose target creature you don't control. Each creature you control deals 1 damage to that creature." (CR 120.3, 608.2c).
# Bot1 has a Memnite and an Ornithopter; on turn 3 it casts the Case (Mox Pearl and Mox Jet) and the trigger's target must be a creature Bot2 controls: Bot1's own Memnite and Bot2's Island are
# refused, and Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2) is chosen (its Memnite is a legal choice too and is left alone). Each creature deals 1 damage, the Ornithopter too though it has no power, two in all, exactly its toughness, and it dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Memnite
Case of the Gateway Express
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Memnite
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Case of the Gateway Express.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
? Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite.Damage = 0
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Gateway Express.Solved = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
